WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.769
Film Courage: Can you think of a moment (let’s
say) the first five years of you living in

00:00:03.769 --> 00:00:06.360
Los Angeles that helped shape your career?

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:13.860
Like I know you had talked about making inroads
or unbeknownst to you that someone you used

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:17.850
to work with remembered you fondly and was
handing your picture.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:24.350
But maybe another story that maybe you weren’t
expecting …it was your first five years

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.560
and it kind of changed things for you?

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:36.760
Robin Riker: Well…I know that something
happened in the first five years that reinforced

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:42.760
my ethic and my sense of integrity in this
town.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:52.460
And it was when a very well-known personality
had taken a shine to me and knew that I was

00:00:52.460 --> 00:01:00.500
looking for an apartment and offered to set
me up in an apartment “no strings attached”

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:09.959
and…well I happen to know a little something
about strings [laughs] and I refused.

00:01:09.959 --> 00:01:12.159
I mean I graciously refused.

00:01:12.159 --> 00:01:18.920
And I mean I met the person at the apartment
to see what it was like and I took a girlfriend

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:22.539
along with me just in case and it was beautiful
and it would have been wonderful!

00:01:22.539 --> 00:01:31.729
But I would have been bought in some way and
still by saying “no thank you” I still

00:01:31.729 --> 00:01:33.509
needed to find an apartment.

00:01:33.509 --> 00:01:42.749
But the power that I felt in (once again)
counting on myself, I’d like to pay my own

00:01:42.749 --> 00:01:50.340
rent and buy my own groceries thank you very
much because that leaves me my own woman and

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:53.599
that was really empowering.

00:01:53.599 --> 00:01:57.659
When I shared that story with some other people
long ago they were like “Are you crazy?

00:01:57.659 --> 00:01:59.189
You could have taken it and…”

00:01:59.189 --> 00:02:00.189
“No!

00:02:00.189 --> 00:02:01.189
I wouldn’t have.”

00:02:01.189 --> 00:02:08.890
It would have compromised me in my world of
morality.

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:13.269
It would have been the wrong thing to do and
so I didn’t do it.

00:02:13.269 --> 00:02:16.260
And again, I had to still find another apartment.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:26.439
But when you believe in yourself and you take
a chance things come and it came.

00:02:26.439 --> 00:02:35.010
Because honestly maintaining your integrity
and your sense of self-worth is the most important

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.090
tool that you have here.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.219
Absolutely the most important.

00:02:39.219 --> 00:02:43.860
It goes back to many other things that we’ve
talked about because if you have faith in

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:48.640
yourself and you know who you are in the world,
it doesn’t matter what anyone else says

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.930
or does because you know who you are.

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:56.760
And often the people who come from the smaller
towns have an even a better sense of who they

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:08.800
are because they grew up in a much less superficial
world where hard work and values were valued,

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:09.800
you know?

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:16.319
So to me that’s your state of mind and your
sense of self-worth are the most important

00:03:16.319 --> 00:03:17.319
things that you can have.

00:03:17.319 --> 00:03:23.459
So that was for me an opportunity to put up
or shut up.

00:03:23.459 --> 00:03:27.590
This is either what I believe or it’s not
what I believe and here’s an opportunity…an

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:33.400
easy way to…it would have been easy, it
would have been very easy to just take that

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:41.810
opportunity but I didn’t…this isn’t
the way you go forward in my estimation.

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:47.840
Film Courage: That’s a real elephant in
the room in terms of the entertainment industry

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:49.549
and it happens to men, too.

00:03:49.549 --> 00:03:50.549
Not just women.

00:03:50.549 --> 00:03:51.840
Robin Riker: Of course it does.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:55.930
Film Courage: And it can happen from other
men or other women, whatever.

00:03:55.930 --> 00:04:03.019
But I think it’s hard for a younger person
who then some how feels very special because

00:04:03.019 --> 00:04:06.480
this person has chosen them and it’s hard
for them to see anything beyond this.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:07.480
Robin Riker: Right.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.480
And we want to be chosen!

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.010
That’s why we come to Hollywood “Choose
me!

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:11.150
See me!”

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.150
You know?

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.150
And temptation.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:14.150
Film Courage: Right.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:16.019
And someone in power [choosing them].

00:04:16.019 --> 00:04:23.470
And I’ve known of people on both sides of
the coin who have gone the way of being taken

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:25.580
care of and there are implications.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.680
I don’t think young people totally realize
this.

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:33.889
Robin Riker: And then…if you got what you
got…did you get it?

00:04:33.889 --> 00:04:41.300
Or was it just given to you because of something
that you bartered with?

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:47.639
And that’s the other thing I say too with
everybody (most everybody) loves to have a

00:04:47.639 --> 00:04:52.120
good time romantically…so I was speaking
at a college at this one point and this one

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:57.630
girl came up to me and said [whispering] “So
what do you think about romance and the casting

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:58.630
couch?”

00:04:58.630 --> 00:04:59.630
And I said “Look.

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:02.860
If you think you would have fun in bed with
this person, have a night out with them, have

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:08.550
a night out with them for that reason alone
but do not think for one moment the you are

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:14.440
going to get something out of it other than
fun because you (no matter what gender you

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:19.330
are, no matter who is interested in you),
you have something that this person can get

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:25.030
anywhere else and they (if there a person
who says they have a job for you or some other

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:30.840
way of elevating you, have something that
only a handful of people have to give.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:35.099
You have nothing to bargain with but if you
think you might have a good time, go ahead!

00:05:35.099 --> 00:05:37.740
But don’t expect anything out of it, you
know?

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:42.341
And that also leaves you in power of your
own life because you made the choice, not

00:05:42.341 --> 00:05:46.090
because something was dangled before you.

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:51.210
But because you decided you would like to
do it because it would be fun, not to get

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:52.210
something.

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:53.210
Film Courage: Right.

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:58.180
And I think there is this whole Scarlett Letter
thing where “Oh…she did this for…”

00:05:58.180 --> 00:06:02.550
and sometimes I can’t always believe it
as it feel like a made up story.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:05.949
That’s the ultimate putting the Scarlett
Letter on someone.

00:06:05.949 --> 00:06:08.509
“Well, this person got this thing because
of doing this.”

00:06:08.509 --> 00:06:09.680
And half the time it’s not even true.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:13.479
Robin Riker: Right and spoken out of jealousy
(like you mentioned before)!

00:06:13.479 --> 00:06:14.479
Film Courage: Right.

00:06:14.479 --> 00:06:17.199
And it could be that the other person actually
did something similar.

00:06:17.199 --> 00:06:24.890
It’s an interesting thing that goes around
and it’s not openly talked about but it

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:26.889
exists.

00:06:26.889 --> 00:06:30.009
I agree with what you’re saying.

00:06:30.009 --> 00:06:34.379
If [a decision to be in a relationship] is
not about any type of barter trade agreement

00:06:34.379 --> 00:06:38.629
[laughs] then that is one’s personal choice.

00:06:38.629 --> 00:06:44.879
But surviving the gossip of “this person
did this, for that” is a very toxic thing.

00:06:44.879 --> 00:06:45.879
Robin Riker: No.

00:06:45.879 --> 00:06:46.879
You don’t want that.

00:06:46.879 --> 00:06:48.389
Again, I don’t want that on me.

00:06:48.389 --> 00:06:49.389
Get that off of me!

00:06:49.389 --> 00:06:51.120
Film Courage: And remaining upbeat and finding
hobbies.

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:52.199
Robin Riker: Right.

00:06:52.199 --> 00:06:53.389
Living your life!

00:06:53.389 --> 00:06:54.949
Live your life everyday.

00:06:54.949 --> 00:06:59.709
Try to do something everyday that has nothing
at all to do with show business.

